🧠 Thoughtline  Local memory for game projects

Quick: [S]ave  [/]search  [M]emories  [I]nbox


                                   Welcome — no memories yet                                    

        Thoughtline remembers the gamedev decisions you'd otherwise forget. Try:

        scene-pattern   — how you wired a Unity / UE5 / PlayCanvas scene
        perf-gotcha     — the GPU stall that took you a day to find
        pipeline-step   — the FBX → glTF → engine import you almost wrote down

        Save your first one from the CLI:
          $ tl save --type perf-gotcha --title "dx11 instancing" --content "…"

        Or from Claude (MCP):
          > Save this to Thoughtline as a scene-pattern
            (calls tl_save automatically)

        Then press r here to refresh.

↑↓ select · enter open · r refresh · q quit